  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Police Professionalization and Community Policing in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) - Phase VI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase VI of the project will continue with the existing model of training existing police officers in community policing, constructing and equipping police stations and substations to house only those newly trained officers, training judicial police officers (JPO), and establishing and/or supporting Local Security Committees. This phase will complete the community policing coverage in Mbuji-Mayi and in Annexe District in Lubumbashi. Construction will implement INL expert-level inputs based on recent inspections from prior phases and fund renovation upgrades in previously-constructed buildings. This phase will also train additional officers to staff stations and sub-stations to strengthen the projects long-term sustainability as the project finalizes work in Mbuji Mayi and Lubumbashi and will be handed over to the government of the DRC. As the new three-month JPO training curriculum (designed with INL and European Union technical support) was officially adopted by the national police, this phase will extend training, expand to Goma and Bukavu, and increase the number of JPOs trained. To address the prevalence of trafficking in persons and sexual and gender-based violence, as well as low female participation rates, the training will include a significant number of participants from the Child Protection and Sexual Violence Prevention Squadrons.</narrative>
  </description>
